  "stage": "board-and-device-planning",
  "visit": 4,
  "text": "`check_constraints` still fails, and the remaining failures are outside what I can change in this stage. I'm stopping here.\n\nI rewrote `design.xdc` with the board's pin lines for `clk`, `led[1:0]` and `sfp_tx_disable`. I added output delays on the LEDs and `sfp_tx_disable`, with a comment above them (the FDA-CON-5 and FDA-CON-11 rules). That cleared the FDA-CON-11 error on the delay line.\n\nTwo kinds of failure remain:\n\n- **FDA-CON-7 on `clk`:** The checker rejects `clk` as \"neither a master-XDC port name nor a bus of one.\" That line is the one `board_constraints` generated from the board resource `clk_25`, so I did not edit it. The spec names the port `clk`, and the board's own resource names are `clk` and `clk_25`.\n- **FDA-CON-8 on the `core: rst`, `h_we`, `h_re`, `h_addr`, `h_wdata` and `h_rdata` ports:** `spec.yaml` lists these under the top-level `ports:`, but they are the core's internal register-bus ports. The top is only meant to have `clk`, `led` and `sfp_tx_disable`.\n  - The fix is in `spec.yaml`: move those ports to the core, or drop them from the top's port list. The entry `core: rst` is also not a valid port name.\n  - I can't edit `spec.yaml` in this stage, and there is no RTL yet.\n\nI did not run `check` with `[\"all\"]`, because the constraint check is still failing and there is no RTL to check yet.\n\nDONE"
 },
